  "details": "would help a lot if it were possible to configure the graphics within the game itself, not outside it.\n  In addition to putting a new option to completely disable people's avatars, tordando them invisible, so it would consume much less processor and ram.\n  Another possible configuration would be the implementation of a configuration to choose between keep or not, the shadows of the game, because the maps that I create, have this option, and this greatly increases the fps, between 10 to 20 fps more.\n  Another idea would be to put a button to disable the interaction with portals, since there are people putting portals on top of others on purpose\n \n                                             these are some of my ideas to further improve this game\n ",
